   "Advisory-only twin review (:advisory-only? true; simulated consent never counts as real consent), grounded in ratified docs/VALUES.md (CID 2b6d6a6a794ef168a00184faf35d3b77efb083c24671e3ff1092a432405f9448) and individual agency to act and object. BIP-020 (CID e7092a361cb03522aa3dc9c4eff85102926cc71ea83c583a4fb7729cffed374a) targets the exact right failure class—you cannot act on or object to delivery you cannot see—but adopting it as written leaves four critical prod loopholes: (1) Intent-vs-wire telemetry illusion: pure core (bitecho.light-node.core/exec-broadcast) already hardcodes mesh_submitted=true before boundary shells touch a wire, while exec-status ignores (:diagnostics state) in favor of (:conn-diagnostics state). Meanwhile, browser_main.cljs routes :p2p-broadcast? P2P-only whenever any P2P channel is open, silently catches .send errors, fires unawaited relay fetches, and returns ok:true + chatHistory :status :sent before routing; node_main.cljs returns ok:true queued:true on failed send; exec-send seeds :created-ms/:last-sent-ms from (:epoch state 0) instead of wall-clock ms (skewing RTO and unacked_aged); and evicted_by_reason omits :capacity-overflow and :expired. Similarly, wait-event's event-matches-wait-filter? is duplicated outside .cljc core and filters on broadcast_seq which handle-wire-broadcast never emits, while control.json omits the daemon's active events-out path. (2) Dishonest browser meshConnected & missing auto-redial: browser_main.cljs get-status and shell/browser.cljc transition-conn keep :phase :open and meshConnected=true when pc.iceConnectionState is disconnected/failed before DataChannel onclose fires, send-sealed-message mutates split-authority :conn, and keepalive clearInterval leaves 0/6 peers with zero bounded backoff auto-redial, zero visibilitychange wake-redial, and zero periodic HTTPS /relay/v1/poll fallback. (3) Weak generator realism: Sections 4.1/5 specify static fanout and ring-buffer properties instead of Malli/test.check stateful command-sequence models over 6-peer ICE cascades, stale-generation callbacks, dead-mesh sends, partial P2P/mesh dual-fanout, outbox evictions, and watcher filter-drops. (4) Unquantified soak & consent loopholes: N=10,000 epochs must explicitly bar silence-as-consent (GOVERNANCE.md requires unanimous 5/5 consent on exact 64-char :patch-cid and 3-runtime :bundle-sha256 with zero :pending), pause on stalled finalized_epoch, bind to extension-by-objection, and require verifiable delivery acks rather than outbound ok:true; Section 5 lacks numeric staging soak thresholds and Rule 6 co-commit gates.",
   :amendments
   ["Split pure-core intent from shell-confirmed transport outcomes in Pillars 1-2 and Sections 4.1-4.2: never increment mesh_submitted or return ok:true / chatHistory :sent until mesh DataChannel or awaited HTTPS /relay/v1/submit confirms admission (emitting counted :diagnose {:reason :mesh-submit-failed} and loud UI/CLI errors on failure); fix exec-send/outbox timestamps to separate wall-clock ms from epoch; include :capacity-overflow and :expired in evicted_by_reason with an explicit numeric unacked_aged threshold; merge (:diagnostics state) into exec-status/getStatus; unify wait-event filtering inside pure .cljc core attaching broadcast_seq and emitting received_but_not_emitted; and persist the daemon's canonical events_out path in control.json/status so CLI --events-out mismatches fail loudly."
    "Make browser liveness and recovery strictly honest in shell/browser.cljc and browser_main.cljs (Rules 4-5): compute meshConnected=false whenever all peers lack BOTH open DataChannel AND healthy ICE/connection state; eliminate split-authority :conn writes in send-sealed-message; enforce dual-fanout (mesh + P2P) in route-browser-envelope! with zero silent catch blocks; add pure generation-tagged bounded backoff auto-redial (reset on open, re-triggered on visibilitychange visible) plus periodic HTTPS /relay/v1/poll + /relay/v1/chain-state fallback when mesh peers are 0/6 (surfacing relayFallbackActive separately from meshConnected); and prove 6-peer ICE cascade -> honest meshConnected=false -> loud send failure -> auto-redial -> post-restore sealed-offer delivery in a blocking headless Chrome E2E gate."
    "Upgrade Rule 1 TDD from static fanout/ring-buffer checks to Malli-validated clojure.test.check stateful command-sequence models before core/shell edits: generate interleaved 6-peer ICE cascades (iceConnectionState failing prior to DataChannel onclose), stale-generation callbacks (gen < current), dead-mesh send/broadcast rejections, mixed P2P + mesh-only dual-fanout with partial P2P link drops, outbox retries/overflow/skew evictions, and ctl wait/wait-event cursor/subnet filter-drops, paired with a non-vacuity MUT-* check proving pre-fix behavior silently drops or misreports."
    "Enforce Sociocratic Stage 2 & staging soak discipline per VALUES.md and GOVERNANCE.md: publish full 64-char CIDs for dist/bips/bip-020-DRAFT.edn, :patch-cid, and 3-runtime :bundle-sha256; bind N=10,000 epochs explicitly to unanimous 5/5 consent (zero silence-as-consent, zero :pending, paused during finalized_epoch stalls, extension-by-objection with mandatory rollback/remediation on :paramount-objection, and clock start gated on verified SACK/watcher delivery proof); quantify Section 5's bitecho-gentoo-lab staging soak (>= 150 epochs / >= 25 min, full 6/6 rolling validator restarts, mixed P2P+mesh subscribers, 0 silent drops, 0 uncounted evictions/filter-drops, bounded 256-entry ring buffer RSS stability); and co-commit docs/SPEC.md, docs/CHANNELS.md, skill/SKILL.md, and cli_flag_inventory_test.clj (Rule 6)."],
