   "BIP-020 (CID e7092a361cb03522aa3dc9c4eff85102926cc71ea83c583a4fb7729cffed374a) diagnoses real agency failures -- in Bitecho, you cannot act on or object to a governance round you silently never receive (Values CID 2b6d6a6a794ef168a00184faf35d3b77efb083c24671e3ff1092a432405f9448). However, adopting it as drafted institutionalizes false delivery proof across four Axiom invariants: (1) Fanout & Outbox Accounting Split-Brain: bitecho.light-node.core/exec-broadcast currently hardcodes mesh_submitted true, p2p_direct false, and a synthetic (max 1 ...) peers_targeted before shell I/O runs, while exec-send returns ok true at queue time (max-outbox-size 64, evicting silently after retries >= 5). Simultaneously, browser_main.cljs/route-browser-envelope! skips validator mesh whenever open-chans is non-empty and swallows .send errors, node_main.cljs one-shot --relay-url skips P2P, and handle-serve-line! swallows mirror-to-relay! and transport exceptions. Pillar 2 cannot truthfully report mesh_submitted or p2p_direct until pure command intent is separated from Rule 4 shell-confirmed :fanout-result effects, browser_main.cljs/send-sealed-message migrates from :conn to :mesh-conns, and new bounded telemetry/ring-buffer keys are reconciled with bitecho.shell.browser/allowed-persistence-keys. (2) Watcher & ctl status Honesty Gaps: core/exec-status omits core [:diagnostics] counters (:outbox-evicted, :subnet-mismatch-dropped, :epoch-skew-dropped, :broadcast-duplicates-dropped, :event-queue-overflow), filters inbox_direct_count/inbox_broadcast_count on :type tags never set by handle-wire-sealed-msg/handle-wire-broadcast, and both Node (node_main.cljs) and JVM (shell/light_node.clj) start-control-server! omit events_out from control.json while exec-wait and /ctl wait ignore subnet_id/session_id/min_broadcast_seq/after_ts and event-matches-wait-filter? drops non-matching events with zero received_but_not_emitted tracking; browser parity also lacks a client-side onEvent/buffer-drop counter. (3) Governance Round Proof Loophole: starting the Stage 2 N = 10,000-epoch clock on directed-session delivery without signed session-ack delivery receipts, received_but_not_emitted == 0 watcher proof on bitecho.org/team, explicit 5/5 unanimous consent (zero :pending per docs/GOVERNANCE.md and validate-bip-receipt), and stall/objection clock pauses recreates silent exclusion under formal cover. (4) CID & Scope Discipline: incident traces (seq 248, seq 606, seq 609, 6-peer ICE cascade) lack 64-char CIDs, the target .md path violates GOVERNANCE.md Stage 1/2 .edn/.patch + Rule 6 SKILL.md/cli_flag_inventory_test requirements, Pillar 4 conflates pure bitecho.hive.twin-stage1 with a runtime :diagnose consumer, and Staging/Chrome E2E lack numeric soak thresholds and a real browser runner.",
   :amendments
   ["AMENDMENT 1 (Rule 4 Fanout Truth & Browser Parity): Decouple pure command :fanout-intent from shell-confirmed :fanout-result effects across light_node.core, node_main.cljs, shell/light_node.clj, and browser_main.cljs; emit mesh_submitted, p2p_direct, per-leg peers_targeted, and counted :diagnose failures only from post-transport Rule 4 reductions. Remove P2P-only exclusion in route-browser-envelope! and one-shot --relay-url, stop swallowing WebRTC/relay (mirror-to-relay!) errors, route send-sealed-message via :mesh-conns and execute CLI :effects, and allowlist bounded Pillar 1-3 telemetry keys in shell/browser/allowed-persistence-keys without persisting live connection state."
    "AMENDMENT 2 (Honest Diagnostics, control.json, & received_but_not_emitted): Expose core [:diagnostics] drop/eviction counters alongside :conn-diagnostics in exec-status and browser get-status, tag :inbox items :direct/:broadcast deterministically on admission, publish canonical events_out in control.json and /ctl status across both Node and JVM daemons so wait-event loudly surfaces path mismatches, align filter semantics (subnet_id, session_id, min_broadcast_seq, after_ts) across exec-wait, /ctl wait, wait-event, and Browser streams, and increment a first-class received_but_not_emitted counter partitioned by reason (filter-mismatch, queue-overflow, cursor-skip, admission-drop)."
    "AMENDMENT 3 (Cryptographic Governance Delivery Proof & Clock Guardrails): Gate the Stage 2 N = 10,000-epoch clock start per member on a verifiable bitecho.org/team delivery-proof bundle (directed session-ack CID + zero unacknowledged outbox-evicted + received_but_not_emitted audit), require explicit 5/5 unanimous affirmative receipts (zero :pending, zero silence-as-consent per docs/GOVERNANCE.md and validate-bip-receipt), and mandate automatic clock pause/extension on stalled epochs, delivery gaps, or any recorded objection."
    "AMENDMENT 4 (CID Verification, Pure Layer Separation, & Quantified Soak/Browser Gates): Pin 64-char SHA-256 digest CIDs for all cited incidents (seq 248, seq 606, seq 609, 6-peer ICE trace) and co-commit GOVERNANCE.md Stage 1 .edn / Stage 2 .edn+.patch artifacts plus Rule 6 SKILL.md and cli_flag_inventory_test updates. Keep bitecho.hive.twin-stage1 strictly pure Sans-IO (consume runtime :diagnose streams in twin_runner / verification harnesses). Gate Stage 2 on a quantified bitecho-gentoo-lab soak (>= 6h or >= 500 epochs injecting >64 outbox saturation, retries >= 5 eviction, dead-mesh recovery, 6-peer ICE churn, mixed P2P+mesh+relay topologies, and --events-out mismatch with 0 uncounted drops), a real headless Chromium E2E suite separate from :test-cljs (:target :nodejs), and Rule 1 test.check stale-generation failure-injection suites."],
