   "Advisory Blind Round-1 review, grounded in individual agency to act and object (docs/VALUES.md CID 2b6d6a6a794ef168a00184faf35d3b77efb083c24671e3ff1092a432405f9448), supports BIP-020 (CID e7092a361cb03522aa3dc9c4eff85102926cc71ea83c583a4fb7729cffed374a) on Rule 5 delivery telemetry and dual-fanout, but flags four unresolved operator-agency gaps that block safe Stage 2 opening (N = 10,000 epochs): (1) Sleeping/restarting catchup & broadcast backfill: BIP-020 hardens live P2P/mesh paths while leaving sleeping, suspended, or restarting peers blind. On /relay/v1/poll (core/protocol/relay.cljc), the 256-slot / 24h / 16 MiB broadcast ring omits min_available_broadcast_seq so waking peers silently jump evicted history, next-broadcast-seq is relay-local (causing :relay-watermark-reset or skipped events across multi-relay failover), and parked long-poll wakeups (shell/http.clj) bypass sub-filter-set and omit last_broadcast_seq. Daemon reconnect (shell/light_node.clj) swallows poll errors and only pushes outbound recovery; sender outboxes evict after retries >= 5 and handle-wire-payload drops pre-session envelopes beyond max-epoch-skew = 15; browser connect-mesh skips /relay/v1/poll when relay-url is nil, stores unscoped localStorage watermarks, skips acks on broadcast-only polls, and swallows poll errors (including post-restore nil :private-key). Starting the N = 10,000 consent clock on send rather than confirmed peer catchup violates agency to act/object. (2) ctl wait / wait-event cursor continuity: ctl wait-event aliases wait against an in-memory 256-entry :event-queue whose exec-wait mixes monotonic event_id and envelope :seq against one threshold, destructively drops queue items on read, and lacks subnet filters, while standalone wait-event tails events.jsonl from EOF (missing restart/reconnect gaps) and swallows append-event-jsonl! errors. Both shells ignore --block (_block?), and control.json records only port/token/pid with no events_out field to power the proposed --events-out mismatch check. (3) Populated sorted-map compatibility: core.cljc emits (into (sorted-map) ...) for :petnames/:sessions and shell/browser.cljc preserves (empty v) on restore, yet browser_main.cljs resolve-peer-target calls (get (:petnames node) (keyword target)), crashing on string-keyed sorted-map lookup misses. (4) Pre-Stage-2 smoke & CID gates: scripts/smoke_light_node_live.sh only tests status on an empty mktemp -d --state-dir, and BIP-020 cites artifacts (dist/bips/bip-020-delivery-telemetry-proposal.md, VALUES, seq 248/606/609) without an automated HTTP 200 + full 64-char SHA-256 verification gate before Stage 2.",
